{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds","id":1528252,"title":"Kuei-jin in Yin/Yang Worlds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-09T03:04:25-08:00","id":1528252,"title":"Kuei-jin in Yin/Yang Worlds","content":"In terms of a cross-chronicle that has all of the World of Darkness races available, how would you treat Kuei-jin in the Yin/Yang worlds?<br /> According to KOTE, <i>&quot;Kuei-jin in the spirit worlds use the spirit Traits of Rage, Gnosis and Willpower to accomplish tasks; utilizing them in a manner identical to spirits themselves (p. 210). For Kuei-jin, Rage equals P\u2019o, Gnosis equals Hun, and Willpower remains identical.&quot;</i><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/B51swcc.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So here's the thing, according to WtO, wraiths do not play by Gnosis/Rage, but they have an actual sheet.<br /> How would you treat Kuei-jin in the spirit world in that case? Also, do they also happen to be immaterial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T05:48:57-08:00","id":1528257,"title":"","content":"Those stats are actually mapped out quite well to Ghosts in the context of KotE if you're running simplified things (which I'd honestly suggest). Rage is P'o is Angst. Gnosis is a bit more tricky, but you could just use Gnosis refluffed as Pathos. Willpower is Willpower. If you're keen on actually using full crossover rules, you're gonna have a special kind of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T10:03:07-08:00","id":1528270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528257#post1528257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those stats are actually mapped out quite well to Ghosts in the context of KotE if you're running simplified things (which I'd honestly suggest). Rage is P'o is Angst. Gnosis is a bit more tricky, but you could just use Gnosis refluffed as Pathos. Willpower is Willpower. If you're keen on actually using full crossover rules, you're gonna have a special kind of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, achieving full crossover rules is something we strive for! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What I fail to understand though, is how actions are going to be performed in the Yin/Yang world?<br /> So let's say a Kuei-jin player would like to strike a wraith for instance, are they going to have to roll their Willpower (instead of Dexterity + Brawl) and then use their P'o as their Strength rating for that matter? Even if that's the case, how soaks would work for instance?<br /> I hope you understand where the confusion stems from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T11:08:12-08:00","id":1528271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528270#post1528270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, achieving full crossover rules is something we strive for! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What I fail to understand though, is how actions are going to be performed in the Yin/Yang world?<br /> So let's say a Kuei-jin player would like to strike a wraith for instance, are they going to have to roll their Willpower (instead of Dexterity + Brawl) and then use their P'o as their Strength rating for that matter? Even if that's the case, how soaks would work for instance?<br /> I hope you understand where the confusion stems from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under these assumptions, yes, you would use WP. However, these rules are an awful lot like the old &quot;use Gnosis to soak in the Umbra&quot; rule for W:tA - a standout inconsistency that eventually got dropped. Given that KotE is based on that set of rules with regard to how it resolves the Umbra (with ghosts compressed into the W:tA setup most likely to save space), you could probably just dispense with rolling Rage, Gnosis, or Willpower and just use Traits.<br /> <br /> If you are going by Revised rules, though, Chi would take a hit. Pre-Revised spirit Power was typically way higher, and Revised made it a step down, while also requiring spirits to spend less of it, so that it could more closely function as a spirit's true health track. Essence was typically the sum of Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, though some spirits had it higher, in some cases far higher for very potent spirits like bigger Nexus Crawlers. A lot of Charms also functioned differently with regard to how Essence was used, so you'd need Revised or W20 texts to make that work and the Vampire Revised Storyteller's Handbook for the KotE update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T14:44:33-08:00","id":1528285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528270#post1528270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, achieving full crossover rules is something we strive for! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What I fail to understand though, is how actions are going to be performed in the Yin/Yang world?<br /> So let's say a Kuei-jin player would like to strike a wraith for instance, are they going to have to roll their Willpower (instead of Dexterity + Brawl) and then use their P'o as their Strength rating for that matter? Even if that's the case, how soaks would work for instance?<br /> I hope you understand where the confusion stems from.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Saur Ops has mentioned, the Wan Guei act in the spirit worlds like Werewolves do. Thus they use their own traits for rolls, the Spirit stats are just shorthand for the denizens of the Umbrae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T07:40:14-08:00","id":1528357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528271#post1528271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under these assumptions, yes, you would use WP. However, these rules are an awful lot like the old &quot;use Gnosis to soak in the Umbra&quot; rule for W:tA - a standout inconsistency that eventually got dropped. Given that KotE is based on that set of rules with regard to how it resolves the Umbra (with ghosts compressed into the W:tA setup most likely to save space), you could probably just dispense with rolling Rage, Gnosis, or Willpower and just use Traits.<br /> <br /> If you are going by Revised rules, though, Chi would take a hit. Pre-Revised spirit Power was typically way higher, and Revised made it a step down, while also requiring spirits to spend less of it, so that it could more closely function as a spirit's true health track. Essence was typically the sum of Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, though some spirits had it higher, in some cases far higher for very potent spirits like bigger Nexus Crawlers. A lot of Charms also functioned differently with regard to how Essence was used, so you'd need Revised or W20 texts to make that work and the Vampire Revised Storyteller's Handbook for the KotE update.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528285#post1528285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Saur Ops has mentioned, the Wan Guei act in the spirit worlds like Werewolves do. Thus they use their own traits for rolls, the Spirit stats are just shorthand for the denizens of the Umbrae.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thank you both for the insightful answers!<br /> <br /> Though I must say that I'm still wondering about the following:<br /> <b>1.</b> Provided we work with the normal rules of WTO and they have fully fleshed-out character sheets, how would you approach powers like this?<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/dMkGn18.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> After all, why would anyone not be able to regularly use Intimidation or Subterfuge against a Wraith to begin with?<br /> <br /> <b>2.</b> Since the book draws similarities between Kuei-jin and Spirits, I was wondering if they are also considered immaterialized? Or that's something that happens only with Yin/Yang Prana at Rank 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T07:51:26-08:00","id":1528358,"title":"","content":"The &quot;provided that she can see them&quot; caveat leads me to believe that the Mantle powers don't need to be used when you're actually in the Umbra, as such; the character could be peering across the Gauntlet or Shroud instead, among other circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T08:23:04-08:00","id":1528359,"title":"","content":"Well all forms of spirits are immaterial by default. To exist in the real world they either need to possess someone or materialise. Some might have a power that allows them to commune accross the Gauntlet/Shroud, but thats a minority of them.<br /> <br /> By default the Wan Guei cannot interact with spirits. They can see them with the Yin/Yang sight, but would need to cross or use specific powers to interact with them.<br /> <br /> Yin mantle is one of these powers that allows you to work on the other side without going there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T18:28:33-08:00","id":1528404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528359#post1528359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well all forms of spirits are immaterial by default. To exist in the real world they either need to possess someone or materialise. Some might have a power that allows them to commune accross the Gauntlet/Shroud, but thats a minority of them.<br /> <br /> By default the Wan Guei cannot interact with spirits. They can see them with the Yin/Yang sight, but would need to cross or use specific powers to interact with them.<br /> <br /> Yin mantle is one of these powers that allows you to work on the other side without going there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, yeah that makes a lot more sense now.<br /> As for the immateriality, I know that all forms of spirits are immaterial, but I meant for the Kuei-jin after crossing the Shroud.<br /> Are they also considered immaterial as well in there? The reason that I'm asking is because I know they add the rating of their Yin Virtue to their Health Levels while in the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T01:08:37-08:00","id":1528410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528252-kuei-jin-in-yin-yang-worlds?p=1528404#post1528404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you, yeah that makes a lot more sense now.<br /> As for the immateriality, I know that all forms of spirits are immaterial, but I meant for the Kuei-jin after crossing the Shroud.<br /> Are they also considered immaterial as well in there? The reason that I'm asking is because I know they add the rating of their Yin Virtue to their Health Levels while in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Materiality is only an affair of the real world. It's something a spirit needs to have a form in the real world. Once you are in the Umbra you are there and anything that exists there has a form that you can interact with.<br /> <br /> When you are physically in the Umbra you do not exist in the real world. You are not a spirit nor do you have charma to incarnate on the other side. You use rituals and/or specific powers to just cross between worlds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}